atent codes and observed scores, and center local trust regions on high-scoring evaluated anchors. Generate a new ephemeral candidate pool each round by uniformly choosing latent-token blocks to perturb inside those regions, inverse-decode the perturbed points, and locally reject invalid, previously evaluated, or duplicate molecules before using posterior Thompson samples to choose the announced batch. Returned scores update the surrogate, anchors, and trust-region state. The corpus supplies only representation learning: no corpus molecule is retrieved, ranked, or treated as a fixed candidate, and every oracle proposal is a newly decoded de novo molecule selected to raise terminal Top-1.","method_tags":{"acquisition_mechanism":"Gaussian-process posterior Thompson selection over a freshly generated trust-region candidate pool","learning_mechanism":"offline corpus-only SeqFlow training plus a task-local latent Gaussian process fit only to oracle-evaluated molecule-score pairs","paradigm":"bijective latent-space Bayesian optimization","proposal_mechanism":"evaluated-anchor trust-region perturbation of latent token blocks followed by inverse-flow de novo decoding","representation":"SELFIES token sequences mapped to an exactly reconstructible continuous latent space by an autoregressive normalizing flow"},"method_references":[{"title":"Lee, S., Park, J., Chu, J., Yoon, M., and Kim, H. J. (2025). Latent Bayesian Optimization via Autoregressive Normalizing Flows. International Conference on Learning Representations 2025.","citation":"Lee, S., Park, J., Chu, J., Yoon, M., and Kim, H. J. (2025). Latent Bayesian Optimization via Autoregressive Normalizing Flows. International Conference on Learning Representations 2025.","url":"https://proceedings.iclr.cc/paper_files/paper/2025/hash/df4f371f1f89ec8ba5014b3310578048-Abstract-Conference.html","kind":"paper","supports":"SeqFlow-invertible trust-region latent Bayesian optimization"},{"title":"MLVLab, NFBO: official PyTorch implem